    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A successor state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> founded c. 1441 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haci-i-giray">Haci I Giray</a>, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>.</li><li>From 1475 an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and ally, its cavalry raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Poland-Lithuania</a> and Muscovy fed the slave market of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Caffa</a>.</li><li>Russian victories made it a nominally independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1774, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a> annexed it in 1783.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Muscovy kept paying the Crimean khans regular ‘gifts’, in effect tribute, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-constantinople-1700">Treaty of Constantinople</a> in 1700, long after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> had vanished.</p></aside>
    </section>

